# Fleeing a fight started from narration makes for the location's way out, on the map.
#
# Out of the fight is not yet out of the location: the party walks from where it fought to the way
# out (the exit glyph on the location map), and anybody standing in an area on the way could still
# stop it there (cli/system/runaway_route.cli covers that). With nobody in the way the walk ends the
# visit, as fleeing always did.
#
# The fight is entered by the attack verb (see cli/verb/attack/success.cli for the flag reasoning).
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --location-type test --location-id 0 --npc-static --start-area "Test Hall" --period dawn --observe-only brewer

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

strategy succeed
goal attack
advance 12 180

click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180

click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180

# The landed attack HOLDS the fight so its first blow can be read (see "Opening a fight: the first
# blow"). The fight opens on the press that closes the segment, not on the swing.
click button
wait mode Fighting 90
fight-end runaway

# Back on the world map: the walk out played (instantly under --cli) and asked for the exit.
wait mode WorldView 90
expect-no-state pois Corpse

quit
